    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0793" n="759" xml:id="pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/12–947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State,
                        at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-09T19:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Telmar 58. For Secretary Marshall from Lovett. Re Martel 52, December 9.<anchor
                        n="31" xml:id="d291-f1"/> All statements to Congress re appropriations for
                    Germany, including Royall’s yesterday, have asserted intention of requiring
                    repayment as first charge. It is expected that aid to Germany under ERP will not
                    be grant but will be a claim against German economy to be settled from excess of
                    exports or in peace treaty. Some repayment may be possible, particularly because
                    of absence of German foreign debt, assuming no other claims are given priority.
                    However, more important is value of this claim in treaty negotiations as basis
                    for keeping other claims down.</p>
                <p>Germany was enemy and we cannot make grants while using loan procedure with
                    former allies. We would have difficulty justifying appropriations for Germany if
                    result was to make jjossible payment current reparations to Russia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d291-f1" n="31" xml:id="d291-f1-content">
